  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "For a reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> the half lives are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> when the concentration of reactant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>=</mo></math> respectively. The order of the reaction is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The relation between half-life and initial concentration of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi>th</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;order reaction can be written as follows,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msub><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mn>100</mn></mfenced><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>50</mn></mfenced><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>order&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>For the second order reactions half-life is inversely proportional to initial concentration.</p></blockquote>",
